window.docContents[90].resolve({"/Standards-Reference-___-PKC-beside-ISO-80000-1-and-the-VIM/The-sources___-and-what-was-checked/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Standards-Reference-___-PKC-beside-ISO-80000-1-and-the-VIM--The-sources___-and-what-was-checked":{"contents":"Each column is a specific document, and a locator in a column was read in that document.\n\n* Dybkær (2009) — An Ontology on Property for Physical, Chemical, and Biological\nSystems. The sections are the ones the documentation comments of the Lean sources\ngive. Where a declaration's comment names no section, the cell says so; none was added\nfor this chapter.* ISO 80000-1:2022 — Quantities and units — Part 1: General, second edition.\nRead in full. Its clause 3 defines no terms of its own: it states that the terms and\ndefinitions of ISO/IEC Guide 99 apply. Guide 99 is the VIM, so for a defined term the\nnormative locator is the VIM 3 column, and the ISO column gives the clause of the\nrunning text (4.1 the concept of quantity, 5 dimensions, 6.2 units and numerical\nvalues, 6.3 mathematical operations) where the standard uses the concept. Its scope\nstates that the ISO/IEC 80000 series does not yet cover ordinal quantities and nominal\nproperties.* VIM 3 — JCGM 200:2012, International vocabulary of metrology — Basic and general\nconcepts and associated terms, third edition, as published by the BIPM (also issued as\nISO/IEC Guide 99:2007). Read in full for the clauses cited.* VIM 4 2CD — the second committee draft of the fourth edition, dated 2023-07-31,\nthe edition the @[vim4 …] annotations of the\ncross-reference chapter use. Read in full for the clauses\ncited. It is a draft: its numbering and wording can change before publication. Each of\nits entries prints the corresponding VIM 3 clause, and the two VIM columns below follow\nthat concordance.\n\nThe first edition, ISO 80000-1:2009, restated the Guide 99 entries in its own clause 3\n(3.1 quantity, 3.2 kind of quantity, 3.9 unit of measurement, and so on). That\nedition is withdrawn and the second edition has no such entries, so a reference to\n\"ISO 80000-1, 3.x\" for a term is a reference to the 2009 edition only.\n\nA dash means that no corresponding term or passage was found in the source. \"No term\" or\n\"no entry\" beside a locator means that the concept appears there in running text or in a\nnote, not as a defined term.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Standards Reference — PKC beside ISO 80000-1 and the VIM","header":"34.1. The sources, and what was checked","id":"/Standards-Reference-___-PKC-beside-ISO-80000-1-and-the-VIM/The-sources___-and-what-was-checked/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Standards-Reference-___-PKC-beside-ISO-80000-1-and-the-VIM--The-sources___-and-what-was-checked"}});